From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Xun2202 <98207886+Xun2202@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 14:10:42 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(ui): align toolbar modes sheets and resized pager
 gestures

Shared navigation components and regression with Mihon 0086. User reports preview.35 feels much better and requests consistent regular/selection/search toolbar geometry. Keep selection cancel/count on the left, categories in the middle and compact actions on the right, retaining category scroll state. Use one compact toolbar height and icon allocation across contexts, remove search field body padding, and animate only the separate equal-height search category row with the existing protected animation clock. Detect actual active search rather than an inactive tab retained query. Pin source/extension/migration management navigation, preserving actual source browsing and the Anikku feed behavior. Isolate dialog navigation locals, draw bottom sheet backgrounds to the window edge and apply system/IME bottom insets once inside the content; retain centered tablet sheets and fork dismissal behavior. On pager width changes cancel the previous user mutation with PreventUserInput and snap the nearest valid page, also aligning restored partial pages; height-only changes keep ordinary gestures. Cover all native pagers in the two apps. Add real Compose toolbar/animated-row/window-inset/pin ownership and held-drag resize/height-only/restoration regressions. No device visual acceptance or quantitative FPS gain is claimed.
